────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PARITY SUMMARY (web → native)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The web source wraps a section/widget/chart in a React error boundary so one render failure
inside it does not blank the whole page, with three fallback modes:
  • DEFAULT  → <ErrorBoundary inline>  : AlertTriangle + "Component failed to load" + error.message
                                          + a working Retry.
  • fallbackTitle → custom headline alert + t('errors.section.subtitle',
                    'Other parts of the page should still work.')  — NO Retry.
  • fallback → caller-supplied node — NO Retry.
The single web t() key is errors.section.subtitle (reproduced verbatim, key + English value).

Native surface (SwiftUI, Apple HIG) reproduces all three modes (SwiftUI has no render-time
try/catch, so the "caught" signal is supplied by the host exactly like the atomic
TSSectionErrorBoundary's hasError flag — this surface is the state-complete peer of that atomic):
  phases    : loading (skeleton) / empty (friendly card) / content (render children) /
              caught (inline | title | custom fallback).
  axis      : connection live/stale/offline → freshness chip + one-shot stale auto-refresh.
  P1/S8     : SectionErrorBoundaryModel state-holder + source seam (no HTTP in the view).
  P1/S9     : design tokens only (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius), no Tailwind ports.
  P1/S10    : SectionErrorBoundaryStrings facade; every string a key (no English literals in code).
  P1/S11    : view.opened diagnostics (surface slug "SectionErrorBoundary") + section.error.caught
              keyed by the boundary `name` (web componentDidCatch [ErrorBoundary:name]).
  a11y      : combined VoiceOver fallback label, individually-labelled Retry/freshness controls,
              Dynamic Type fonts, reduce-motion via the shared TSFadeIn/TSSkeleton primitives.

